<title>USA: US Treasury 5-yr notes seen yielding 6.31-6.32 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 5-yr notes seen yielding 6.31-6.32 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $11.5 billion in 5-year notes on Wednesday should produce a yield around 6.31 to 6.32 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>Bidding is expected to go fairly well, dealers said.</p>
<p>Just before the bidding deadline of 1300 EDT/1700 GMT, the 5-year notes were trading with a when-issued yield of 6.313 percent.</p>
<p>Results for the auction are expected around 1345 EDT/1745 GMT.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
</text>
